{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>Other elohim.</b> Entities distinct besides El, blessed be He." "<b>Or to the sun or to the moon.</b> For they are corporeal." "<b>Which I have not commanded.</b> Which I have not appointed with any delegated appointment, such that they could do as they please; rather, I have given them a fixed decree that shall not be transgressed. The opposite is what idol worshippers think, who suppose that over every city there is a ruler able, as he pleases, to do good or harm, and that he does good when they worship him."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:21:38.730753724Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}